            <div xml:id="d891">

                <pb facs="0923" n="915" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg915"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5 Construction/200: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-27T18:00:00+01:00">June 27, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 27—2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>563. My 535, June 20, 5 p.m.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d891-f1"/> Protocol will be
                    signed at noon on June 30. Australia, New Zealand, India and Canada will not
                    sign <pb facs="0924" n="916" xml:id="pg916"/> as they did not participate in the
                    discussions leading up to the escalation agreement. The Foreign Office will,
                    however, deliver to the American and French Embassies four official
                    communications on behalf of those Governments to indicate their concurrence. The
                    British will at the same time deliver a note to the American Embassy, the text
                    of which will follow that communicated in the Embassy’s 476, June 2, 8 p.m. On
                    the same day the British and Germans will sign a protocol but no word has yet
                    been received from Russia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
